ping, so a failed ping does not prove a host is down."}],"w4-1":[{"k":"matrix","t":"chmod 750, as a grid","x":["Read","Write","Execute"],"y":["Owner","Group","Others"],"c":[[["Yes","good"],["Yes","good"],["Yes","good"]],[["Yes","good"],["No","bad"],["Yes","good"]],[["No","bad"],["No","bad"],["No","bad"]]],"n":"Each digit adds read (4), write (2) and execute (1): 7 = 4+2+1, 5 = 4+1, 0 = nothing."}],"w4-2":[{"k":"flow","t":"Patch management","s":[["Find available updates"],["Test them","an update can break other software"],["Deploy in order of risk"],["Verify they worked"],["Record it all"]]},{"k":"hub","t":"What a log entry tells you","c":["One log entry"],"s":[["When","accurate time from NTP links events across systems"],["What happened","for example event ID 4625, a failed logon"],["Who","usually, the account"]]}],"w4-3":[{"k":"flow","t":"How a firewall reads its rules","s":[["A connection arrives"],["Rules are checked in order"],["The first matching rule decides"],["No rule matched: denied","implicit deny","bad"]]},{"k":"hub","t":"Hardening: shrink the attack surface","c":["Before the long trip"],"s":["Remove software you don’t use","Close ports you don’t need","Change default credentials","Apply patches","Start from a secure baseline"]}],"w4-4":[{"k":"flow","t":"Threat, vulnerability, risk","s":[["Vulnerability","an unlocked window"],["Threat","a burglar in the area"],["Risk","the chance they come through, and what it would cost","warn"]]},{"k":"compare","t":"Where you may practise","cols":[{"h":"Allowed","tone":"good","items":["Systems you own","Your own lab and virtual machines","Practice environments that explicitly authorize testing"]},{"h":"Never","tone":"bad","items":["Anything you do not have written permission to test","Scanning or probing other people’s systems"]}]}],"w5-2":[{"k":"compare","t":"Category is how; type is what it aims to do","cols":[{"h":"Category: how","items":["Technical","Managerial","Operational","Physical"]},{"h":"Type: aims to","items